@startuml sequence_catalog_fetch
!theme plain
' Compact layout (tuned per diagram — see README, 'Sequence-diagram layout').
hide footbox
title Catalog Fetch – UI Dynamic Form Construction

participant "Setup Page\n(Streamlit)" as Setup
participant "api_client\n(httpx)" as Client
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "Catalog\n(deap_pettingzoo.catalog)" as Cat

== First render: fetch full catalog ==

Setup -> Client: GET /catalog
Client -> API: HTTP GET
API -> Cat: catalog.to_json()
Cat --> API: {catalog_version, algorithms[],\n environments[], coevolution,\n budget_modes[], availability}
API --> Client: 200 JSON
Client --> Setup: catalog dict
Setup -> Setup: cache in st.session_state

Setup -> Setup: render Environment tab\n(selectbox: env names from catalog)
note right of Setup: show availability badges\n(missing extras greyed out)

== Env selection -> compatibility check ==

Setup -> Setup: user selects environment

Setup -> Client: GET /catalog/compatibility?\n  env=simple_tag_v3&algorithms=ea,cma-es,maddpg,...
Client -> API: HTTP GET
API -> Cat: compatible_algorithms(env, all_algos)
Cat --> API: {matrix, compatible[], incompatible[]}
API --> Client: 200 JSON
Client --> Setup: compatibility matrix
Setup -> Setup: render Algorithm tab\n(compatible highlighted, incompatible disabled)

== Algo selection -> param rendering ==

Setup -> Setup: user selects algorithms

loop for each selected algorithm
    Setup -> Client: GET /catalog/algorithms/{name}
    Client -> API: HTTP GET
    API -> Cat: get_algorithm(name)
    Cat --> API: AlgorithmSpec {hyperparameters: ParamSpec[]}
    API --> Client: 200 JSON
    Client --> Setup: algorithm spec
    Setup -> Setup: render hyperparameter widgets\n(number_input, selectbox, toggle, ...)\nper ParamSpec {type, min, max, choices, group, advanced}
end

== Coevolution options ==

alt coevolution tab active
    Setup -> Client: GET /catalog/coevolution
    Client -> API: HTTP GET
    API -> Cat: coevolution options
    Cat --> API: {modes[], schedules[], samplers[], eligible_optimizers[]}
    API --> Client: 200 JSON
    Client --> Setup: coevolution options
    Setup -> Setup: render coevolution form\n(sides, mode, schedule, k_opponents,...)
end

@enduml
